[10] When using the textbook's rules below, the delay must therefore include both the phase delay from propagation and the phase changes from reflection along the two paths, not just the extra distance traveled inside the film.
Expressing this total phase difference as an equivalent distance, using the wavelength in the same medium at the comparison point, gives the effective delay used here;
