[14] The same wavelength here also means the same frequency, while a constant phase difference means that one wave's lead or delay within the oscillation cycle does not keep changing relative to the other wave.
The waves reflected from the outer and inner surfaces of the oil film are **two parts of the same light beam**, so they can retain a shared phase relationship.
